{"id": "86301", "name": "Cubic_1", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p>Determine a complex root of the cubic equation \\[ {{CT:0}} = 0.\\] Hint: the answer should be given in the form \\(p + qi\\). <br /> [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p class=\"input-hint input-hint-complex\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.88em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0;text-align:left\">How to enter: the imaginary unit \\(i\\) is typed as the letter <code dir=\"ltr\">i</code> (or <code dir=\"ltr\">%i</code>), and multiplication with a star. For example <code dir=\"ltr\">3-2*i</code>.</p>", "generalfeedback": "<p>Firstly, look for a real root by dividing the equation by \\({{CT:1}}\\) where \\(a\\) is a factor of the constant {{CT:2}}.</p>\n<p>In this case \\(a = {{CT:3}}\\) is the appropriate value.</p>\n<p>Hence dividing {{CT:4}} by {{CT:5}} gives \\[{{CT:6}}\\] Using the quadratic formula \\[x=\\frac{-b±\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\] for the equation \\(ax^2+bx+c\\) gives \\[x= \\frac{{{CT:7}}±{{CT:8}}}{{CT:9}}\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore \\( x = {{CT:10}},{{CT:11}}\\)</p>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "argument", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 2, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "expandans1:expand(ans1);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans1"